    "On American commodity exchanges, traders dumped corn futures today in panicky trading, as a steady bout of selling in the morning turned into a rout after mid-day. Sellers were said to be spooked by low oil prices, which have steadily cut into demand for ethanol as a gasoline substitute and, as an additional crushing blow, the enactment of new legislation by Congress that will sharply reduce subsidies for ethanol production.": "在美国商品交易所，交易员今天在恐慌性交易中抛售玉米期货，早上的稳定抛售在中午后变成了溃败。据说卖家被低油价吓坏了，低油价稳步削减了对乙醇作为汽油替代品的需求，而作为额外的沉重打击，国会颁布的新立法将大幅减少对乙醇生产的补贴。",
