    "This raises an interesting possibility for our marketing strategy: We should begin making extraordinary efforts to acquire elderly clients over the age of 80, the older the better, for our banking and trust services. As many of these individuals, if not already experiencing senile dementia, soon will be, they will be ideal targets for high-pressure marketing of services they don't need, at very lucrative, above-market rates.": "这为我们的营销策略提出了一个有趣的可能性：我们应该开始非常努力地为我们的银行和信托服务获得80岁以上的老年客户，越老越好。由于这些人中的许多人，如果还没有经历老年痴呆症，很快就会经历，他们将是高压营销他们不需要的服务的理想目标，以非常有利可图的、高于市场的费率。",
